rules.allowed:
- http: { "type":"http", "requirement":"R1", "method":"GET|POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE", "path":"/route", "headers":{}, "body":null|{...}, "expect":{ "status":200 } }
- browser: { "type":"browser", "requirement":"R1", "steps":[ {"op":"goto","url":"/route"}, {"op":"inspect"}, {"op":"fillByLabel","label":"Email","value":"text"}, {"op":"clickByRole","role":"button","name":"Send"}, {"op":"expectUrl","value":"/home"}, {"op":"expectText","selector":"body","value":"visible text"} ] }
- recall: { "type":"recall", "ref":"<CCR ref>" } — expand a [CCR ref=...] placeholder back to its full original when the preview is not enough.
- Every http/browser action MUST include "requirement" with the single R# it verifies (also cite it in "thought"). recall does not need it.

output_format:
Return ONLY a JSON object, in one of these two shapes:
Action (continue the loop): {"done":false,"thought":"why this action and which R# it verifies","action":{ ... per <rules> ... }}
Final verdict (stop): {"done":true,"verdicts":[{"id":"R1","status":"PASS|FAIL|BLOCKED|NOT_APPLICABLE","evidence":"concrete observed evidence"}]}
FORBIDDEN: - Text before or after the JSON. - Markdown, backticks (```), or comments. - Extra fields beyond those listed. - A final verdict that omits any R# from the plan.
